1111:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\note
1112:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\          - PE (Parity error), FE (Framing error), NE (Noise error), ORE (OverRun
1113:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            error) and IDLE (Idle line detected) flags are cleared by software
1114:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            sequence: a read operation to USART_STS register (USART_GetFlagStatus())
1115:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            followed by a read operation to USART_DAT register (USART_ReceiveData()).
1116:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\          - RXNE flag can be also cleared by a read to the USART_DAT register
1117:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            (USART_ReceiveData()).
1118:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\          - TC flag can be also cleared by software sequence: a read operation to
1119:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            USART_SR register (USART_GetFlagStatus()) followed by a write operation
1120:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            to USART_DAT register (USART_SendData()).
1121:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\          - TXE flag is cleared only by a write to the USART_DAT register
1122:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            (USART_SendData()).
1123:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\          - RTO flag is cleared only by a write 1 to the USART_CTRL2.RTOCF bit.
1124:../../../firmware/n32h7xx_std_periph_driver/src/n32h7xx_usart.c **** *\*\            (USART_ClrRTOFlag()).
